= Discovery 33: Ore-Christol Algebraic Transcendence

Christol's Theorem (1979) proves that a bit sequence $c(t)$ is $p$-automatic if and only if its generating series $F(X) = sum c(t) X^t in FF_p[[X]]$ is algebraic over the rational function field $FF_p(X)$. By Ore's Lemma, any algebraic series satisfies an equation of the form:
$ sum_(i=0)^d A_i(X) F(X)^(p^i) = 0, quad A_i(X) in FF_p[X], quad A_0 eq.not 0. $
Over $FF_2$, $F(X)^(2^i) = F(X^(2^i))$. We constructed the exact Ore matrix of size $M times K$ (where $K = (d+1)(D+1)$ unknowns) and solved for non-trivial nullspaces via Gaussian elimination:

